From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROCKNIX Team <admin@rocknix.org>
Date: Sun, 13 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: force S16_LE only for compressed playback

The backend fixup forced S16_LE for all streams. PCM playback then lost
resolution after software volume: at low volume the audio distorted.
Let PCM streams negotiate the format.

Taken from ROCKNIX (projects/ROCKNIX/devices/SM8250/patches/linux/0100).

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -121,7 +121,14 @@
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	channels->min = channels->max = 2;
-	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+
+	/* Only force S16_LE format for compressed playback */
+	if (rtd->dai_link->compr_ops) {
+		/* This is a compressed stream, set format to S16_LE */
+		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+	} else {
+		/* For other streams, let format be negotiated as before */
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
